vrend: read constant buffer 0 bound as a buffer into the default uniforms

A guest binds the constant buffer 0 of a shader either as inline constants
(SET_CONSTANT_BUFFER) or as a buffer resource (SET_UNIFORM_BUFFER). A shader reads its
constant buffer 0 from the default uniform block (fsconst0[] and the like), which vrend
fills only from the inline constants, and vrend binds UBOs only for the buffers from 1:
a buffer bound at index 0 was never seen by the shader, and its constants stayed zero.

Mesa's vl_compositor binds the colour matrix of an RGB to YUV conversion that way, so
with the virgl driver the conversion (scale_vaapi from RGB to NV12 in FFmpeg, which
KRDP uses) multiplied by a zero matrix and wrote zeros: a solid green picture.

Remember when the constant buffer 0 is set whether it is a buffer, and at the draw read
it (glGetBufferSubData) into the uniforms with glUniform4uiv. It is read at every draw,
since the guest can write to the buffer without binding it again. The conversion then
writes what Mesa's matrix gives: the luma of a ramp goes from 0 0 0 to 0 124 255. What
is left is Mesa's: the graphics path of vl_compositor_convert_rgb_to_yuv() never loads
an RGB to YUV matrix, and the one that is sent is the YUV to RGB matrix of the
compositor's initial state.

